          "id": "SP_BATHYPOLYPUS_SPONSALIS",
          "name": "Bathypolypus sponsalis",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Bathypolypus sponsalis",
          "lineage": "Bathypolypus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Bathypolypus sponsalis, commonly called the globose octopus, is a deep sea cephalopod that can be found in both the eastern Atlantic Ocean and the Mediterranean Sea. It possesses many morphological traits adapted to a deep sea environment, including large eggs, reduced gills, no ink sac, and subgelatinous tissues. A distinguishing factor are the relatively large reproductive organs.",
